{"t": 1794106639.6233478, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "INCIDENT: PaymentGatewayErrors / checkout (AG-7731)\n\nWhat happened: checkout's charge payload was rejected by the payment gateway with HTTP 400 invalid_amount \u2014 \"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\". The gateway moved to API version 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\"), so decimal EUR amounts are no longer accepted; this caused the 4xx rate to jump to 38%.\n\nFix: checkout/gateway.py charge_payload() now converts amount_eur to integer cents (Decimal, half-up) and sends {\"amount\": <int cents>, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}. 12.34 -> 1234. Fractional cents are rounded half-up; flag if the gateway expects a different rounding policy.\n\nNext: deploy checkout with this change and watch gateway 4xx rate; ack/resolve AG-7731 once the error rate is back to normal."}, "ok": true}
